# [Before you start]($heading.id('before-you-start'))

- Use a Linux or macOS development machine with Git and internet access for the
  first build. See [Hardware compatibility]($link.page('zml/user-guide/reference/hardware-compatibility').unsafeRef('build-with-zml')) for the
  framework's build targets.
- Install [Bazelisk](https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazelisk#installation) as
  `bazel` on your `PATH`. On macOS with Homebrew, run `brew install bazelisk`.
  Bazelisk reads `.bazelversion` from the ZML checkout and selects Bazel for you.

# [1. Get the ZML source]($heading.id('get-the-zml-source'))

```sh
git clone https://github.com/zml/zml.git
cd zml
```

Run the remaining commands from the checkout root.

# [2. Run MNIST]($heading.id('build-and-run-mnist'))

`bazel run` builds the target as needed and launches it with the pretrained
weights and test images.

[]($section.attrs('bazel-platforms'))

```=html
<div class="bazel-preflight">
  <div class="bazel-backend" hidden>
    <label for="mnist-backend">Backend</label>
    <select id="mnist-backend" aria-describedby="mnist-host-requirements"></select>
  </div>
  <strong>Host requirements</strong>
  <p id="mnist-host-requirements" class="bazel-platform-host" role="status">Linux x86-64 or macOS (Intel or Apple Silicon). CPU is enabled by default.</p>
</div>
<div class="bazel-platform-shell command-shell" data-bazel-target="//examples/mnist">
  <pre><code class="sh" data-bazel-command="run" data-copy-label="Copy MNIST run command">bazel run \
  --@zml//platforms:cpu=true \
  //examples/mnist
</code></pre>
</div>
```

# [3. Read the prediction]($heading.id('read-the-prediction'))

```=html
<figure class="bazel-prediction">
  <pre><samp><strong>✅ RECOGNIZED DIGIT:</strong>
+-------------+
|   #######   |
|   #    #    |
|       #     |
|      #      |
|     #       |
|     #       |
|     #       |
+-------------+</samp></pre>
  <figcaption>Sample prediction. Compare it with the input image printed in the terminal. The example picks a random image each run.</figcaption>
</figure>

<details>
  <summary>Build only</summary>
  <div class="bazel-platform-shell command-shell">
    <pre><code class="sh" data-bazel-command="build" data-copy-label="Copy MNIST build command">bazel build \
  --@zml//platforms:cpu=true \
  //examples/mnist
</code></pre>
  </div>
</details>

<details>
  <summary>Optional framework test</summary>
  <div class="command-shell">
    <pre><code class="sh" data-copy-label="Copy framework test command">bazel test //zml:test</code></pre>
  </div>
</details>
```

